# 8/24/26 Moving and geese!
Right now I'm in the middle of a move. I say the middle because I'm currently in a gap between leases and staying with my mom (thanks mom). I had to move everything to a storage unit, and I'll have to move everything back out of the storage unit once the lease for the new place starts. It's annoying to have to move twice and have a gap, but the new place is going to have a LOT more space and it'll be in a quieter area.

My old place was a 1 bedroom that I shared with my partner. My desk was in the living room, and my partner's desk was in the bedroom. In the new place we'll still share a bedroom, but we'll each have our own separate offices! I really want to have 2 desks, one desk for my computer and a work desk for soldering/writing/whatever other hand creating.

I've been spending a lot of time with my mom since I'm staying at her place (and she works from home). So today we went out to go feed geese some watermelon, corn, and oats. I brought my camera and took some pictures of the geese!

Here's a big photo dump of the geese:

